===Question #9===
{{Cquote2|What player stage do you think this boss most appeals to? Does this match what you envisioned when you first tested the boss?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-OhtpdX3pZk&t=2877s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' It depends on what you mean by where it should sit. You can do the boss post-quest on an 85 combat account - base 75. It is possible, but with every boss, it’s more efficient to go train your stats up as high as you reasonably want to and make money in other reasonable pieces of content and farm it.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' That goes for literally everything in the game! It’s more efficient to get max combat and then kill Giant Mole than it is to struggle to go dry at Mole at base 60. You can kill Mole with base 60, but I do think it’s reasonable to go there, do your 50-100 kills, maybe get the Ancient Sceptre for an upgrade and then drop it for a bit and come back when you’ve got better gear.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I don’t expect mid-level players to sit there for hundreds and hundreds of kills trying to farm out the Venator bow or the pet. I’d say it all depends on what you want from the boss. If you only want a couple of things, I think it’s completely reasonable for mid-to-late-game. If you want to farm the pet and multiple Venator Bows for money, then I would expect that to be more for the late-game players in a proper endgame, because the gear matters a lot there.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I think that’s a good thing - gear should matter a lot in every piece of content. I think it’s a shame if you’re getting the exact same kills per hour with a whip versus a scythe. The scythe should be better - it should feel good. You want to incentivize it to get better gear.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I think it’s completely fine to kill it earlier on, but I wouldn’t recommend farming it for hours. I would say the same for minibosses or Vorkath. Barrows is the exception because you don’t need gear there - gear just doesn’t matter. You get a trident or an Iban and you’re almost getting max kills per hour there. The difference isn’t as big a deal going from rune platebody to full ancestral - it’s 100mil for very, very little DPS in the grand scheme of things.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' For here, the difference between Ahrim’s and a trident versus ancestral and Shadow is monumental. It’s so big, but I don’t think that’s a problem.
* '''Mod Bruno:''' I’ve seen some players say that it’s like a mid-level boss, and I don’t really know where they got that from. I don’t think we’ve called it a mid-level boss, and I don’t think it’s fair to compare it to a mid-level boss.
* '''Mod Bruno:''' When I hear mid-level, I see something like Barrows or Sarachnis, those sorts of bosses where you don’t really need that much to do it efficiently, whereas here you do need a little bit of skill and some good gear. I’d say it's aimed more towards high-level, but not exactly endgame or anything like that.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' If I remember correctly when we put it out there in terms of expected difficulty to begin with, we didn’t give any information at all. Later on we then compared it to a more mechanical version of Vorkath with lower stats. Vorkath is not exactly a mid-game boss in its own right with the requirements is has.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' We did also state that you could defeat the boss with 85 combat - it was listed in the blog itself as well and confirmed that you can do it. It’s as Arcane said; probably not the best thing to farm long-term if you don’t have high combat and high gear, but that’s the nature of bossing!
* '''Mod Arcane:''' People are very divisive over what is mid-game. Some people say that Vorkath is mid-game - it comes from a grandmaster quest! Vorakth isn’t Inferno, but that doesn’t make it mid-game. The differences between early-game, mid-game, late-game and endgame is so vague and there isn’t anything official. It’s very subjective.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' Since Vorkath is mechanically simpler and has higher requirements to get to, the distinction gets caught up around that, but I still wouldn’t farm Vorkath with budget gear. There’s just no point. I’d wait until I got decent gear, just like I would do with Muspah.

===Question #10===
{{Cquote2|What is your reasoning behind dropping the Venator Shards more often and needing 5 to create the bow than just making the bow a drop that's 5 times as rare?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1w4LJiW-7I&t=2344s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' I just wanted to try something different. Having a singular rare drop is more exciting - you have the high variants where you could complete the entire Bow in one kill. That’s exciting; the potential, the idea that you can get a T-Bow from one KC.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Then you have the other side of it. The chance of going three times dry on something is a 1/20. If you’re thinking about it from the entire player base, or even your friend group - if you’ve got 20 friends that play RuneScape, one of you is likely to go three times dry.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' If you’re in the context of Lizardmen Shamans, for example, going 15k Shamans dry for a warhammer, it’s depressing. I just wanted to try something different. If you give out smaller, more frequent quantities of an item, you’re statistically more likely to complete it in an average range. You’re less likely to finish it early, but you’re less likely to finish it later. It averages out and decreases the variance.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' That’s good and bad - it means you can’t go as dry, but you also can’t be as spooned. I wanted to try it to see what players think; do they prefer this style of drop? It’s not dropping anything crazy. It seemed like a good chance to try it out and see what people think.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I’m looking for feedback on that, there probably won’t be much feedback until you’ve gone dry on it, but maybe after a couple hundred KCs, give me a message. I’m genuinely curious. We’ll see how it goes. Maybe this is something we take forward to have a bit of a balance. You don’t want an entire drop table that’s all shards - that’s not very exciting - but maybe some of the rarer drops should be broken up. We’re doing an experiment, and we’ll see how it goes.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' The initial reaction seems relatively positive. People are saying they like it and prefer it that way!

