* '''Mod Bruno:''' The way the boss works is that it goes from one phase to the next, to the next. If you try to skip one of those phases, it may not work properly and bug out in some way. We’ve tried to fix it by making it so that if the boss reaches zero HP whilst it's trying to transition to the next phase, it will regen a little HP and then carry on properly.

===Question #13===
{{Cquote2|Damage is currently nulled between phase transitions near the end of the fight. Can this be fixed?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1w4LJiW-7I&t=2549s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' Damage nulling is really bad. It was really annoying at Vanguards and it was annoying at Nex - I don’t know if this still happens at Nex; we went back and forth on that for ages. Generally, damage nulling is really bad, but for this, I feel it has to null it because it’s going from regular hitpoints to Prayer hitpoints.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' It’s a completely different health bar. These are completely different mechanics, so it has to null it here. You can just use that period where you’re transitioning or the explosion attack is just about to end to eat instead - you know exactly when it’s going to happen so you can time it. Hopefully, it’s not too frustrating - for here, it has to null the damage.

===Question #14===
{{Cquote2|Can the devs give any insight into what goes into designing drop tables for bosses? Why so many skilling supplies?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1w4LJiW-7I&t=2628s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' We’ve had a lot of criticism in the past where drop tables are really boring. We only really have about three types of items we can give out - alchables, skilling resources like seeds or ore, or we can give raw GP. We don’t really have a lot of diversity.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We can give alchables on every drop table, but that introduces a lot of Gold into the game, and that’s really boring. So we try and put a few skilling materials in there. That can be okay, but if you really rely on skill materials, you end up really hurting the economy.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Say we had one boss that only dropped ranarr weeds. The ranarr weed economy would be devastated. So what we try to do now is spread it out - we get a little bit of seeds, we get a little bit of herbs and a little bit of ores. We try to hurt everything ever so slightly, because no matter what drops, it hurts the economy in some way by adding more things into the economy that we’d want to take out more than we want to put in.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Bosses are generally about “okay, people are going to be eating food and drinking Prayer pots and super combats. They’re the resources that are the most consuming by bossing. We want to make sure that people are consuming an adequate amount of resources, and not generating too much.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' It’s about trying to get the balance right and not introduce too much of an individual item from any single piece of content. We want to spread it out so it doesn’t hurt anything. Sometimes we get that wrong, “oops, we gave out way too many ranarr seeds on this drop table, we need to change that”.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' That’s what we did today. We pulled back on some of the resources slightly - it still may be giving you a bit too much; we’ll see about that, but we don’t want to have any knee-jerk reactions. We’re pulling it back a bit.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Most of the Muspah drop table is quite varied and spreads it out. There are some seeds on there; sure, they’re not very common, but maybe it’s giving out just a few too many of them. This is what we tweaked today. Maybe we didn’t get it right - we can pull it back a bit more, but we have to give out some things - alchables, skilling supplies or uniques.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We don’t want it to drop nothing, and we don’t have to have too many empty drops where you would get three pure essence. Drops that are effectively ‘dead drops’ feel really bad, so it’s a balance of making sure we give a player something that makes them feel like their time wasn’t wasted and haven’t gotten a net loss on supplies, while also making sure we’re not giving out too much of any individual resource that would hurt the economy too badly. It’s difficult, there’s not a lot of flexibility.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Something that we’ve been trying to do in the last two updates is introduce new resources. For example, we’ve introduced the ancient essence, where we could have used something else like blood shards instead. Generally, if we introduce a new resource, it gives us another option of something to drop for a player with a different type of desire.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We’re trying to introduce new resources that we can give out so that we’re not always just giving ranarr seeds and ranarr weeds. That’s also a really good idea that we’ve tried to do, but it’s obviously a little harder to introduce new things.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We can pull back on supplies - in the feedback we’ve seen, the general consensus is that it’s introducing a few too many resources, but we don’t want to just completely hammer the regular drop table because the uniques aren’t particularly amazing on this boss. They aren’t going to be holding 100-200mil values. If we really hammer the drop table, it’s going to look really unappealing to do for everyone. It’s difficult - drop tables are really difficult to balance. They’re very back and forth.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' In the four-plus years of working at Jagex in Community Management, I can certainly say that drop tables have been the bane of my life when it comes to feedback on new releases that involve PvM! But it’s just as you say - it’s the nature of the beast.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' I feel like we’ve done a lot better this time around than we have in previous bosses; at least it seems way more on the line of “it could be a little bit broken, it could also be a little bit okay”. I’d rather see that than “holy crap, this is broken and there are a million threads posted, everyone is rushing to the boss, everything is broken” and then we have to change it and everyone gets upset and angry because they no longer make as much money as they did before.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' So I think it’s okay, but we'll continue to monitor it.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I know people are panicking about seed prices plummeting. It’s a valid thing to panic about. There are two major things - one, you’re panicking and the market is completely player-run, so if people think that the boss is dropping a lot of seeds based on some wiki rates or their own experience. You see twelve ranarr seeds dropping and think “wow, that boss drops lots!” word will spread and people will start panic selling. That’s a big factor that makes them crash.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' The second thing is that a lot of people are doing this particular boss right now. It isn’t like some people are doing ToA, some people are doing ToB and there are a lot of people doing various content with their own different drop tables where it’s a lot more spread out. 90% of the community just moves to one boss, so a lot of those drops are going to go down in price. There’s more of this coming in than anything else in the game now.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' It was the same with ToA - as soon as ToA dropped, all of those resources just plummeted because so many people were doing ToA. It’s suffering from success. That will normalise after a couple of weeks. After their 50-100 KCs, people will go back to whatever grind they were doing.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Then the resources will go back to normal and people will stop panic selling. We will monitor it long-term to see if the boss is objectively dropping too many seeds. That isn’t the only factor, however. It’s not just about the drop table.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' That’s a really, really good point to make, and a really important clarification as well. That’s also part of the reason why we don’t just straight up gut the drop table immediately. We made some changes today to slightly reduce the drops because we felt that even with player levels dropping down over time, it would still be a bit too powerful.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' As Arcane said, if we completely gutted it now, then as player activity drops and players lose interest in the boss long-term, it could become something that is just not appealing at all and we want to avoid that.

===Question #15===
{{Cquote2|Can we get a quick start option to instantly spawn the boss, similar to Vorkath? The 30-second respawn timer feels a bit too much since this is a solo boss.}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1w4LJiW-7I&t=3038s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' We could, it depends on how we do it. Nightmare is really obvious; Nightmare goes back to sleep, you kill her and you wake her up again. Vorkath is really simple because he's an undead dragon and he constantly gets revived. Grotesque Guardians has a big bell in the arena that you can ring - some things are easier than that.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I don't really know what this one would be. We could just spawn a random item on the floor that you can just click on. That probably would suffice. I do think stuff like that is generally better so that the player can start the fight whenever they want.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We could look at reducing spawning time, but there was a lot of feedback in playtesting that it's a bit too quick. You have to pick up all your supplies since you kind of get quite a few things. You could get six summer pies drop and two Prayer potions and a ranging pot, that’s a lot to pick up. You have to manage your inventory, heal up and pre-prayer. It can take a lot of time, so we increased it, but the better that players get and the more comfortable they get in that whole gameplay loop, they just end up sitting around waiting.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' You can just leave and re-enter if you want to go really quick, but it's not particularly nice either, especially if you want to leave stuff on the floor.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' That does remove the supplies you've saved and juggling, right? I'm just joking here, but maybe make everyone bring a spade and have to dig the ground up to bring it back out of the ground. That's where it comes from - it's an underground worm thing. That's my useful input of the day!

===Question #16===
{{Cquote2|Could we get the possibility to break down Ancient Icons into Essence? Just like the Venator Shards.}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1w4LJiW-7I&t=3148s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Bruno:''' I wouldn’t be against it.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I’m not overly against it. I don't think it's necessary. - there will be more purpose for ancient icons in the future. So multiple is not useless yet.

===Question #17===
{{Cquote2|Would the J-Mods be interested in adding more Item Clue steps and stashes? Maybe one with the upgraded Ancient Staff and another one where you have to equip a Sun Keris outside of ToA?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1w4LJiW-7I&t=3170s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Bruno:''' I won't mind but it would be a pain, so I'm not inclined to do it. Maybe if there was a new Clue Scroll expansion at some point, then it would make sense for us to add items that weren't out in the last Clue expansion.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I think it's a really good thing for us to do. I just don't know when or why we do it. Is it really random, or do we release a big update, and just add a bunch more clues and stashes? It would be good because it gives more demand for items.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' That’s probably one thing that we need to think about because it always falls back to internal discussions that go ‘’yeah, we'll do a Clue expansion at some point and we'll bundle it up with them”. Then we never do a Clue expansion because everything else comes out instead. I think it's probably worth thinking about when new content comes out going forward, to work out how we might be able to incorporate it.

